From 6e69662127ffb2d45a319f97d40372df213b2700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:36:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 065/145] fixup! drm/meson + dw-hdmi: 10/12-bit deep color HDMI
 output for G12A

Drop the stale meson_encoder_hdmi_detach().

The function was written against a base that predates the meson switch
to the bridge-connector CEC notifier: it dereferences a cec_notifier
member that struct meson_encoder_hdmi no longer has, calls
cec_notifier_conn_unregister() without <media/cec-notifier.h>, and is
never referenced because meson_encoder_hdmi_bridge_funcs has no .detach
entry.  CEC is wired up through bridge.hdmi_cec_dev instead, so there is
nothing for a detach hook to undo.

Fixes three -Wimplicit-function-declaration / no-such-member errors and
a -Wunused-function warning.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
index 693d12cc5bd6..d83b0df95dba 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
@@ -54,14 +54,6 @@ static int meson_encoder_hdmi_attach(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 				 &encoder_hdmi->bridge, flags);
 }
 
-static void meson_encoder_hdmi_detach(struct drm_bridge *bridge)
-{
-	struct meson_encoder_hdmi *encoder_hdmi = bridge_to_meson_encoder_hdmi(bridge);
-
-	cec_notifier_conn_unregister(encoder_hdmi->cec_notifier);
-	encoder_hdmi->cec_notifier = NULL;
-}
-
 /*
  * Bus-format classification.  The VENC->HDMI-TX bus is 3x10-bit
  * natively; what varies per format is the chroma layout and the wire
-- 
2.43.0

